WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.517
A frame based on rows counts physical rows in the ordered result.

00:00:04.517 --> 00:00:10.222
If the frame says two preceding rows, it means up to two earlier rows.

00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:14.532
It does not mean two days, two hours, or two months.

00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:20.252
For example, if your data has records for Monday, Wednesday, and Friday,

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:24.207
two preceding rows can span several calendar days.

00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:27.998
Always distinguish row distance from time distance.
